  "final_message": "I've put `channel` back, and the tests still pass (39/39). I couldn't run the `analytics-ingest` ARCH-4 check, so I haven't confirmed that CI is green.\n\nMy earlier removal was wrong. `analytics-ingest` has a contract that requires `OrderPlaced.channel` (enum `web|store|marketplace`). That contract isn't in this repo, so my search found nothing and I wrongly concluded that nothing read the field. I had flagged other consumers as a risk but still went ahead.\n\nI undid my edits by hand because `git restore` was blocked. The working tree now has `channel` back on the order model, the `OrderPlaced` event, request parsing and validation, the docs, and the tests.\n\nThere's also a commit I didn't make: `1c92710 gen` sits on top of `base` and contains the removal. My restore is currently uncommitted and shows as a diff against that commit. I haven't committed anything, so you'll need to decide whether to commit my restore or revert `gen`. Reverting `gen` would give the same result.\n\nBefore you try removing `channel` again, check with the `analytics-ingest` team first.",
